{"case_id":"T8036","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["configuration","input semantics"],"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["ProtoConverter::evmVersionMapping","EVMVersion::osaka","EVMVersion::allVersions","EVMVersion::fromString","EVMVersion::name","EVMVersion::isExperimental"],"reason":"S1 introduces Osaka as a selectable EVM version, but H0's Program_Version-to-EVMVersion mapping ends at Program::PRAGUE. Consequently, protobuf-generated programs cannot exercise production behavior with EVMVersion::osaka(), including the new \"osaka\" name/fromString semantics and experimental-version classification.","evidence":["S1 adds EVMVersion::osaka() returning Version::Osaka.","S1 adds osaka() to EVMVersion::allVersions(), \"osaka\" to EVMVersion::name(), and Version::Osaka to the version enum.","S1 changes EVMVersion::isExperimental() to return *this > EVMVersion{}, which applies version-order semantics to the newly added Osaka value.","H0's ProtoConverter::evmVersionMapping switch has cases through Program::PRAGUE only and no Program::OSAKA case."],"recommended_action":"Extend the fuzz input protocol with an OSAKA Program_Version value and map it to EVMVersion::osaka(); add fuzz assertions or coverage for Osaka through allVersions(), name(), fromString(\"osaka\"), and isExperimental()."}
